From: vincenzopio <43883474+vincenzopio@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 10:48:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] xgameruntime: Implement XStore's game license, product
 queries and Store ID keys.

XStoreQueryGameLicenseAsync() asks xodus-service for the signed-in account's license to the
title named by StoreId in its MicrosoftGame.config, in the market of the user's region: active,
trial and SKU. An account that does not own the title gets an inactive license; game license
change registrations are accepted, as the license does not change during a session.

XStoreQueryAssociatedProductsAsync() pages through the title's add-ons as the Store's public
catalog lists them (storeedgefd.dsx.mp.microsoft.com/v9.0/products/<id>/addons, 25 a page, the
largest it allows), in the market of the user's region and the user's locale: title, description,
kind, the price as the Store formats it, and one SKU per Store SKU.
XStoreProductsQueryHasMorePages() and XStoreProductsQueryNextPageAsync() follow the catalog's
pages; past the last one the call completes with E_BOUNDS. Every product query result is read the
same way, whichever *Result function a title uses. The Store compresses large answers, so WinHTTP
requests accept gzip and deflate.

Ownership is not in the public catalog, and no Store service answers it for the user's own
tokens (collections.mp.microsoft.com returns an empty list even for the game the account owns):
isInUserCollection stays FALSE, and entitled product queries complete with no products and log
that ownership is unknown.

XStoreGetUserCollectionsIdAsync() and XStoreGetUserPurchaseIdAsync() ask
collections.mp.microsoft.com and purchase.mp.microsoft.com for Microsoft Store ID keys, as the
GDK documentation describes, with the title service's ticket and the user's Xbox token for the
relying party the NSAL names (XUserTokenForRequest()). Tickets and keys are credentials and are
not logged.

The other XStore calls are stubs; asynchronous ones still start and complete with E_NOTIMPL,
because titles wait for the completion (Minecraft stops loading at 41% otherwise). XStoreTests
check contexts and that every call completes; XStoreLiveTests ask for the real license and
products (XGR_LIVE_XBOX=1).

Original work for macrock (LGPL-2.1-or-later).

Topic: xstore
